A||||7||MooCow||Sunroof rattles !!||||8||
Z||000000||MooCow||08-21-2001||10:55 PM||||OOOOOOOOO  diving down the road today and I hear this rattle noise everytime I hit a bump.  So I shut it and it still makes the noise.  I know the noise is comming from the two screw in the front of the sunroof cause I can watch it move.  The thing is that they dont tighten.  All it does is spin and I can get it to tighten.  I shuvved a rubber washer under the black part but it didnt work.  Any ideas here??<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||8
Z||000001||Scott||08-22-2001||11:46 AM||||Go to a Pontiac dealer and order two new hinges (black plastic coated front thingees).  They cost ~$3 each and will help quiet your 'roof.  Also look at the latch, specifically the portion attached to the glass.  There should be a rubber O-ring on each side of the  prongs that connect to the interior latch.  Replace the O-rings & hinges and you should have a quiet sunroof.  If this doesn't work you may have a loose hinge attachment to the roof.  I'd check the rivets at this location too.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||08-22-2001||12:05 PM||||There are no rivets at all.  The only thing that is making the noise is the two front hooks on the sunroof.  They are loose and I can watch the sunroff bounce off of them.  I need to know how to tighten them cause they don't tighten, all they do is spin.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000003||Diamond Joe Quimby||08-22-2001||12:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MooCow:<BR><B>There are no rivets at all.  The only thing that is making the noise is the two front hooks on the sunroof.  They are loose and I can watch the sunroff bounce off of them.  I need to know how to tighten them cause they don't tighten, all they do is spin.<P>Thanks Ken</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ken, I had the same problem. I just replaced the front hooks (they call them tabs at the Fierostore.com), and I also replaced the bushings. I got the bushings from a Pontiac dealer for 87 cents a piece. That solved my problem. While I was at it, it replaced the bushings where the latch attaches to the glass also.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-22-2001||01:43 PM||||On the outside...aren't those black caps?  I think you need to pop them off and tighten them(from there you can get a torx on them)<BR>I don't remember exactly...anoyone know?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||08-22-2001||01:46 PM||||Loose sunroof hinge attaching bolts are the major cause of sunroof leaks according to what Ed Parks told me years ago.  I was ready to replace the sunroof seal when he told me to replace the hinge hardware.  Sure enough it stopped the rattles and the leaks.<P>I got the hinges and the mounting hardware for the hinges and the latch for around $20 US.||||reg||1
Z||000006||MooCow||08-22-2001||10:30 PM||||Yes I poped the black thing off to try to tighten it but I cant.  Noothing will grip it enough to turn.  I need to know how to do this.  The sunroof doesnt leak at all only makes a rattle noise because the right side hinge is loose.  Anyone know how to get the hinges off??<P>Thanks for all the responces,         Ken||||reg||2
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||08-22-2001||10:40 PM||||Hey Ken!<BR>The quickest way to remove the hinge hardware is to tap the edge of the glass with a ball peen hammer...<BR>If you don't want to replace the glass, then with a small torch (pen torch) heat the nuts and see if they come loose (loc-tite)...<BR>If you get frustrated, see step one!!!<BR>Also, using a moto tool, grind a slot in the screw heads, so you can use a driver on it...<BR>BUY THE HARDWARE FIRST!<BR>OOPS! That should have been the first thing I listed, damn!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
